Z||000000||dennis_6||10-14-2001||07:27 PM||||My brother has a white 84 4 cylinder Fiero.  It is his first car.  The engine runs, but will need to be replaced soon.  I think he wants to hold on to car as it is his first.  So my question is if you can put a PCM and a caddy v8 in a 84 Fiero, how hard could it be to splice an 84 4 cylinder and 86 V6 harness together?  I have a degree in electronic engineering, so I belive I can do the work myself.  I really can't see it being to hard to do.  If this does materialize I will put the info on my website to help all the others who want a v6 conversion.<P><BR> ||||reg||12
Z||000001||KRMFiero||10-14-2001||07:31 PM||||Why splice? grab the compete dash back wiring from the 86 car, that way you can use AUX guages and everything, sounds hard but it is pretty simple<P>Kyle||||reg||1
